⟦ fibonacci.vx — Fibonacci sequence in VORTHEX
  Demonstrates recursive functions, conditional branching (⟁),
  stack manipulation, and I/O.

  Algorithm:
    fib(n) = n            when n <= 1   (base case: ⟁ branch NOT taken)
    fib(n) = fib(n-1) + fib(n-2)   when n > 1   (⟁ branch TAKEN → fib_recurse)

  fib_recurse(n) stack trace for n=3:
    ⋄      → [3,3]     dup n
    ∇      → [3,2]     n-1
    fib    → [3,1]     fib(n-1) = fib(2) = 1
    ◈      → [1,3]     swap
    ∇      → [1,2]     n
    ∇      → [1,1]     n-2
    fib    → [1,1]     fib(n-2) = fib(1) = 1
    ⊕      → [2]       fib(2)+fib(1) = fib(3) ✓
⟧

⦿ fib [ ℕ → ℕ | → ]
  ⋄ 1 ≻ ⟁ fib_recurse
⌸0xE6588286
⦾

⦿ fib_recurse [ ℕ → ℕ | → ]
  ⋄ ∇ fib ◈ ∇ ∇ fib ⊕
⌸0x9F4546BC
⦾

⟦ Print fib(0)..fib(10) each on same line, separated by two spaces ⟧
⦿ fib_sequence [ → | → ]
  0 fib print_int «  » ⊞
  1 fib print_int «  » ⊞
  2 fib print_int «  » ⊞
  3 fib print_int «  » ⊞
  4 fib print_int «  » ⊞
  5 fib print_int «  » ⊞
  6 fib print_int «  » ⊞
  7 fib print_int «  » ⊞
  8 fib print_int «  » ⊞
  9 fib print_int «  » ⊞
  10 fib print_int print_nl
⌸0x36C9A274
⦾

⦿ print_int [ ℤ → | → ]
  ⊞
⌸0x83FC135E
⦾

⦿ print_nl [ → | → ]
  «\n» ⊞
⌸0xC4D7783C
⦾

⦿ demo [ → | → ]
  «Fibonacci sequence fib(0)..fib(10):\n» ⊞
  fib_sequence
⌸0x377C0572
⦾

demo
